<title>CANADA: Canfor lumber downtime to reduce output.</title>
<headline>Canfor lumber downtime to reduce output.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canfor Corp said on Monday that downtime at four sawmills would reduce its lumber production by 35 million board feet.</p>
<p>The lumber manufacturer announced on Friday that four sawmills would take downtime starting in mid-June to control overall inventories and help balance volumes under a Canada-U.S. lumber trade accord.</p>
<p>Three of the mills will close for three weeks and one for four weeks. The mills are Netherlands, Isle Pierre, Fort St. James and Taylor in British Columbia.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
